00:09:04.617 --> 00:09:11.397
In New Westminster, a Victorian Gothic house at 239th Street in Queens Park was built in 1888

00:09:11.397 --> 00:09:15.997
and a neighbor is asking the new council to keep it standing. The Vancouver Sun says

00:09:15.997 --> 00:09:19.877
As Marney Ford fell for the house on night walks, and when the four sales sign appeared,

00:09:20.057 --> 00:09:21.517
she went looking for a way to save it.

00:09:21.937 --> 00:09:26.137
In October, she asked Council either to buy and restore it, or to help a group of people

00:09:26.137 --> 00:09:26.537
do that.

00:09:26.977 --> 00:09:30.837
She said the counsellor she met were supportive, and she is waiting to see if this Council

00:09:30.837 --> 00:09:31.537
feels the same.

00:09:32.157 --> 00:09:36.297
Mayor Daniel Fontaine and five new Westminster Progressives counsellors were elected last

00:09:36.297 --> 00:09:37.717
month on financial restraint.

00:09:38.157 --> 00:09:40.637
Only one counsellor outside that slate won a seat.

00:09:40.637 --> 00:09:47.597
The corner lot was listed in August at $1.425 million, and can be bought now for $1.25 million.

00:09:48.097 --> 00:09:54.837
Samuel Boivare, a director at Heritage firm Luxton &amp; Associates, said the firm was hired to write a heritage values assessment.

00:09:55.277 --> 00:10:00.717
The owner is the estate of William Shorty, who lived there from 1970 until his death in 2025.

00:10:01.497 --> 00:10:07.377
Boivare said the city usually asks for this kind of assessment when someone wants to develop a property older than 100 years.

00:10:07.377 --> 00:10:12.977
The house is on the 1986 Heritage Inventory and is protected under the Queen's Park Heritage

00:10:12.977 --> 00:10:15.657
Conservation Area, adopted in 2017.

00:10:16.337 --> 00:10:18.257
It got a water hookup in 1893.

00:10:18.937 --> 00:10:24.197
Boavere links the building boom to the Canadian Pacific Railways' arrival in 1886 and a branch

00:10:24.197 --> 00:10:28.017
line into new Westminster from Westminster Junction, now Port Cook Whitlam.

00:10:28.577 --> 00:10:34.437
Between 1888 and 1892, the city's population more than doubled to 7,500.

00:10:34.437 --> 00:10:39.557
The original lot owner was Methodist Minister Edward White, who arrived in 1859.

00:10:40.077 --> 00:10:42.957
The lot was once much larger and was subdivided over time.

00:10:43.517 --> 00:10:48.017
Boavare calls the house a rare Victorian gothic, drawing on English and medieval styles.

00:10:48.657 --> 00:10:54.377
Rupinder Bossy, Deputy Director of Planning and Development, said the owner has asked about demolition options,

00:10:54.597 --> 00:10:57.177
and the city has no further information about a development.

00:10:57.657 --> 00:11:00.357
The Community Heritage Commission can advise on protection.

00:11:00.837 --> 00:11:02.557
That advice does not bind counsel.

00:11:02.557 --> 00:11:07.737
Ford's request is still a request. The new council has not said whether it will buy the house,

00:11:08.057 --> 00:11:13.937
help a private group buy it, or leave it alone. Also in the paper, TransLink retired the last Orion

00:11:13.937 --> 00:11:19.277
V buses at the end of October, 25 years after they entered service, and double-deckers have

00:11:19.277 --> 00:11:25.297
mostly taken their place on longer highway-style routes among downtown, Richmond, Langley, Coquitlam,

00:11:25.797 --> 00:11:31.277
South Surrey, and White Rock. Eden O'Mahoney's team, in molecular ecology resources this week,

00:11:31.277 --> 00:11:36.817
flew a drone through humpback blow off the BC coast in 2022 and 2023.

00:11:37.397 --> 00:11:43.337
Took 58 samples from 26 whales, found about 84% of the DNA was the whales, saw little

00:11:43.337 --> 00:11:48.677
recent inbreeding, and noted the population fell about 20% from 2012 to 2021.

