00:14:59.996 --> 00:15:04.796
Here's the case on both sides of a tenant rights bylaw. Cope Counselor Sean Orr wants staff

00:15:04.796 --> 00:15:10.276
to study a universal tenant rights bylaw and to look at criminalizing predatory practices by landlords.

00:15:10.376 --> 00:15:12.256
Council has not voted on it.

00:15:12.716 --> 00:15:17.036
Cope campaigned this year on the daily lives of lower income people, renters and working

00:15:17.036 --> 00:15:17.436
people.

00:15:17.896 --> 00:15:20.796
And this week's motions are how the counselors say they will follow that.

00:15:21.336 --> 00:15:26.136
Ours piece is the one aimed at landlord conduct, a citywide tenant rights bylaw, and a look

00:15:26.136 --> 00:15:28.216
at treating predatory practices as crimes.

00:15:28.736 --> 00:15:31.536
On the argument that existing rules are not enough for renters.

00:15:31.976 --> 00:15:35.916
The Goodman report, a local commercial real estate publication, answered on Monday.

00:15:35.916 --> 00:15:40.976
It called the proposal a damaging ideological policy assault on landlords and investors,

00:15:41.356 --> 00:15:44.856
and a governmental sledgehammer that could crush housing investment in the city.

00:15:45.276 --> 00:15:47.856
That is the case against, in that publication's words.

00:15:48.356 --> 00:15:52.856
The cost lands on people who finance rental housing, and the city risks driving investment

00:15:52.856 --> 00:15:53.176
away.

00:15:53.716 --> 00:15:55.476
The motions are being introduced this week.

00:15:55.856 --> 00:15:58.456
